+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Our services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) is that standard, and later features (e.g. JSON Patch, RFC 6902) build on it, so it must be correct and shared.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`: returns the value a JSON Pointer refers to, and throws if the pointer is syntactically invalid or does not resolve to a value of the document.
+- Add an exported `JsonPointerError` (extends `Error`) thrown for both failure kinds, so callers can tell pointer failures from programming errors.
+- Governing standard: RFC 6901 (§3 syntax, §4 evaluation, §5 error handling). Not breaking: nothing exists yet to break.
+- Out of scope: the URI fragment representation (§6, callers must percent-decode first), parsing JSON text, setting/removing values, building pointers, JSON Patch.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: resolving an RFC 6901 JSON Pointer against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code in `src/` and tests run by `npm test`; no runtime dependencies; `package.json` unchanged except what test running needs, if anything.
+- New public API surface (`resolvePointer`, `JsonPointerError`) that importers and later features will depend on.
